<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Shah III Bahmani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1463">1463</a>–<a href="/years/1482">1482</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad Shah III Lashkari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Shah III was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> from 1463 to 1482, succeeding his brother Nizam Shah as a boy. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-gawan">Mahmud Gawan</a> as chief minister the kingdom reached its greatest extent, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a> and pressing to the eastern coast. In 1481, deceived by a forged letter, he ordered Gawan's execution, and he died the following year.</p></div>
